WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.802
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to the show, everybody!

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.371
Welcome to "The Tonight Show"!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:07.673
This is the type
of New York City spirit

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:09.075
you're gonna get.
Welcome, everybody.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.211
-Jimmy!
-I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:13.746
Guys, guess what's finally here.

00:00:13.746 --> 00:00:16.582
The summer Olympics
kick off tomorrow.

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:20.720
This is a big deal.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.922
The official motto
for this year's Olympics

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:25.190
is "United by Emotion."

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:26.993
Yeah, and
the unofficial motto is

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.461
"As of right now,
we're still doing it."

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:33.633
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:35.167
That's right.
Tomorrow's the big day,

00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:37.770
and all of our best athletes
have arrived in Tokyo.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.606
Legends like Simone Biles,
Katie Ledecky...

00:00:40.606 --> 00:00:43.343
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:44.610
...Kevin Durant...

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:46.045
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:48.214
...and a dancing horse
named Butterscotch.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.316
[ Cheers ]

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:52.952
Meanwhile, as if all the COVID
concerns around the Games

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:55.555
aren't bad enough,
a bear was spotted

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.957
inside the softball stadium...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:00.960
...and is still on the loose.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.562
What an Olympics
this is gonna be.

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.464
I mean, between the bears
and getting a disease,

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:07.133
it's like we sent our athletes
to a game of "Oregon Trail."

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.935
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:11.003
It's not a good situation.
Apparently, the bear got really

00:01:11.003 --> 00:01:14.073
agitated after officials made
him sleep on a cardboard bed.

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:16.142
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:18.844
But officials are working hard
to make sure everyone stays safe

00:01:18.844 --> 00:01:20.613
and healthy
at this year's Games.

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:22.949
But some people are still
unclear about what rules

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:25.685
the athletes have to follow
in Olympic Village.

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:29.522
So here to clear things up
is Olympics spokesman Ron Hobbs.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:34.427
Ron?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:36.695
Ron, what is the IOC's
official policy

00:01:36.695 --> 00:01:39.332
on getting together
and socializing in person?

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:41.700
-Jimmy, we'd never tell
these world-class competitors

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.369
what they can or can't do.

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:44.804
We're simply discouraging people

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:48.474
from engaging
in unnecessary physical contact.

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:50.576
-Right.
Maybe you could clarify

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:52.812
"unnecessary physical contact"?

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:54.747
-Simply put, no hanky-panky.

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:55.915
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:58.817
No two-person push-ups.
No knocking boots.

00:01:58.817 --> 00:02:01.153
No boffing, boinking,
buttering the biscuits,

00:02:01.153 --> 00:02:04.423
boom-boom, bouncy-bouncy,
or bow-chicka-wow-wow.

00:02:04.423 --> 00:02:07.360
[ Laughter ]
-All right. Thank you.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.361
Is that -- Is that why the beds
are made of cardboard?

00:02:09.361 --> 00:02:10.763
-Actually,
the beds are just about

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:12.232
sustainability and recycling.

00:02:12.232 --> 00:02:13.832
But if they happen to discourage

00:02:13.832 --> 00:02:15.702
a game of human Tetris,
so be it.

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:16.935
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.935 --> 00:02:19.239
Because there should be
no grown-up nap time,

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:22.575
no baking the potato,
no horizontal hula,

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.944
glazing the doughnut,
greasing the loaf pan,

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:27.112
or squat jumping
in the cucumber patch.

00:02:27.112 --> 00:02:28.814
[ Laughter ]
-All right. I --

00:02:28.814 --> 00:02:32.719
[ Laughter continues ]

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:34.320
I feel like
you're trying to say something

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.122
without really saying it.
And that's...

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:37.590
-Let me rephrase.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.325
No tangling the downstairs
Christmas lights.

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:40.693
-Okay.

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:44.097
-No ordering fries "animal
style" from In-N-Out Burger.

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:46.999
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:49.469
-What?
[ Laughter continues ]

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:51.671
-No making bacon,
making whoopee, or...

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:54.040
♪ Makin' my way downtown,
walking fast ♪

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.707
♪ Faces pass and I'm homebound ♪

00:02:55.707 --> 00:02:59.245
-Yeah, I know -- okay, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:00.813
Maybe you should just tell us

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:02.748
the full list
of what's not allowed.

00:03:02.748 --> 00:03:04.750
-Sure thing.
No rolling in the hay,

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:08.053
no digging up sand crabs,
no dipping the candle wick,

00:03:08.053 --> 00:03:10.556
sweeping the chimney,
opening the Gates of Mordor,

00:03:10.556 --> 00:03:12.725
letting the Joker
in the Batcave,

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:15.194
doing the Monster Mash,
rummaging in the root cellar,

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:17.563
searching for pocket change,
shocking the monkey,

00:03:17.563 --> 00:03:19.331
shrimping the barbie,
shucking the oyster,

00:03:19.331 --> 00:03:22.234
shellacking the canoe,
testing the suspension,

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:24.971
battering the corn dog,
getting busy, getting down,

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:26.773
getting it on,
getting some strange,

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:29.308
getting some
stank on the hang down,

00:03:29.308 --> 00:03:31.577
doing the nasty,
the wild thing,

00:03:31.577 --> 00:03:34.046
or doing the hoody-hoo!

00:03:34.046 --> 00:03:36.082
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:40.453
♪♪

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:44.256
-Sorry. What I meant to say is,
what is allowed?

00:03:44.256 --> 00:03:46.292
-Well, uh,
hand stuff is fine.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:48.394
-Okay, thank you, Ron.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:50.129
[ Cheers and applause ]
Ron Hobbs, everyone.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:54.600
Thank you, very much.
Enjoy the Olympics.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:59.004
-In-N-Out Burger.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.004 --> 00:04:01.107
-Well, that's not all
people are confused about

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:02.475
when it comes to the Olympics.

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:04.176
There's a lot
of misinformation out there,

00:04:04.176 --> 00:04:06.112
so I thought it'd be helpful
to break down what's fact

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:08.046
and what's fiction
about this year's Games.

00:04:08.046 --> 00:04:11.517
For example, Simone Biles
may attempt a Yurchenko

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:15.121
double pike vault
and half-on with two twists.

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:17.523
Fiction,
that's her Starbucks order.

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:18.791
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:20.526
-It's not true.
-Yeah, it's not true.

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:22.695
-Next up,
Facts -- karate, skateboarding,

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:26.332
sport climbing, and surfing,
are making their Olympic debut.

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:28.668
Fiction --
Frisbee golf is next, brah.

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:31.003
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.003 --> 00:04:33.672
And, finally, fact -- the Games
will have no spectators.

00:04:33.672 --> 00:04:35.608
Fiction -- When they heard,
badminton players were like,

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:37.109
"Wait.
You can have spectators?"

00:04:37.109 --> 00:04:38.110
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:42.315
That's fiction.
They know that.

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:45.084
Switching gears, last night,
Fox News aired a 10-second

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:47.220
public-service announcement
urging viewers

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:51.257
to get the vaccine.
[ Audience murmuring ]

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:53.425
Although it didn't help when
they ended the PSA by saying,

00:04:53.425 --> 00:04:55.761
"Just so you know, this could be
the microchip talking."

00:04:55.761 --> 00:04:58.397
[ Laughter ]
[ Scattered "Oohs" ]

00:04:58.397 --> 00:05:00.866
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.866 --> 00:05:04.537
Some tech news.
[ Chuckles ]

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:07.272
I saw that Amazon --
Amazon's Alexa just rolled out

00:05:07.272 --> 00:05:10.810
a male voice assistant,
and his name is Ziggy.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.778
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.778 --> 00:05:14.246
Right now,
Jeff Bezos is thinking,

00:05:14.246 --> 00:05:16.549
"I go to space for 11 minutes
and you name the voice Ziggy?

00:05:16.549 --> 00:05:18.650
What's going on?"
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:21.020
Meanwhile, I heard that Twitter
is testing a new feature

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:25.791
that lets users
upvote and downvote tweets.

00:05:25.791 --> 00:05:27.093
It's great.
It's like executives

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:28.261
looked at Twitter and thought,

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:30.229
"How can we make this place
even more toxic?"

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:31.964
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:33.933
"Your grandma's 90th birthday?"
Enh!

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:35.267
[ Laughter ]

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:36.936
"No, thanks."

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:38.904
Well, this isn't good.
I read that muffins

00:05:38.904 --> 00:05:42.041
sold at Walmart and 7-Eleven
have been recalled

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:45.177
over concerns about listeria.

00:05:45.177 --> 00:05:47.713
Walmart apologized
while 7-Eleven just slapped on

00:05:47.713 --> 00:05:49.715
a sticker that said
"Listeria flavored."

00:05:49.715 --> 00:05:53.719
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:53.719 --> 00:05:58.657
"I'll take two of those."

00:05:58.657 --> 00:06:00.258
And, finally,
this is going viral.

00:06:00.258 --> 00:06:02.894
Teenagers in New Jersey
were celebrating a birthday

00:06:02.894 --> 00:06:05.698
on one of those slingshot rides
at an amusement park

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:07.200
when something
unexpected happened.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.635
Watch this.

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:11.704
-All right.
Happy birthday.

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:14.840
-Bye!
[ Screaming ]

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:16.209
[ Audience "Ohhs" ]

00:06:16.209 --> 00:06:20.112
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.112 --> 00:06:21.680
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:24.450
-What?!
-Wow!

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:26.119
[ Laughter ]

00:06:26.119 --> 00:06:33.091
-What?!
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.091 --> 00:06:35.260
That girl will now go
through her life with a phobia

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:37.363
of not just rides
but birthdays, in general,

00:06:37.363 --> 00:06:39.465
I mean, that's one of
the scariest things --

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:41.400
Can we see that again?
That's insane.

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:43.803
[ Both screaming ]
Oh, my God!

00:06:43.803 --> 00:06:49.875
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.875 --> 00:06:51.677
Afterward, her friend was like

00:06:51.677 --> 00:06:53.746
"Yeah, we're definitely gonna
buy the photo from that ride."

